WEBVTT

1
00:03:29.857 --> 00:03:31.859
Whoa! Hey, hey! Whoa!

2
00:03:32.485 --> 00:03:37.573
Doggone it! Get this piece of junk out
of here, unless you're prepared to drown!

3
00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:39.867
Officer, I'm trying. It's stalled.

4
00:03:40.034 --> 00:03:42.912
Put your vehicle in neutral.
Turn your wheel left.

5
00:03:43.079 --> 00:03:45.873
It's a friggin' mess down here.

6
00:03:46.666 --> 00:03:49.752
So, are we all gonna die?

7
00:03:51.003 --> 00:03:53.923
Yeah, we're all gonna die. Just not yet.

8
00:03:58.511 --> 00:04:00.888
But I am gonna have to let out more.

9
00:04:01.139 --> 00:04:04.267
My worst was sweet 16. I had mono.

10
00:04:05.351 --> 00:04:07.228
What was your worst birthday, Wayne?

11
00:04:07.395 --> 00:04:11.482
Are you kiddin'? Could I possibly
have had a birthday worse than this?

12
00:04:11.649 --> 00:04:15.528
- What kind of loser do you think I am?
- Don't answer that, Phil.

13
00:04:15.695 --> 00:04:19.866
Hank's gonna open a gate. We expect
another surge. Let's move these cars.

14
00:04:23.536 --> 00:04:26.956
Well, hello, gentlemen!
Hey, Wayne. Happy birthday.

15
00:04:27.874 --> 00:04:32.211
Mike, what you're doin'...
I don't know if I'd be here, considerin'.

16
00:04:32.712 --> 00:04:36.632
You would if you wanted the last two
paychecks some bastard owed ya.

17
00:04:36.799 --> 00:04:40.428
I want you to know, I think
the people here made a big mistake.

18
00:04:40.595 --> 00:04:42.763
The people?
You're the one who screwed him.

19
00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:47.435
Mr Mayor, as much as I'd like to stand
here talkin' about how great I am,...

20
00:04:47.602 --> 00:04:50.771
..if you don't move,
I'll have to haul your ass off to jail.

21
00:04:50.938 --> 00:04:52.940
OK, OK. I'm goin'.

22
00:04:53.107 --> 00:04:55.651
Keep up the good work, boys.
It's appreciated.

23
00:04:57.945 --> 00:04:59.947
Asshole.

24
00:05:00.114 --> 00:05:04.202
What do you say we torch that son of
a bitch's house and blame it on looters?

25
00:05:04.368 --> 00:05:07.413
Or how about puttin' a dead cow
in his living room?

26
00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:12.293
He comes back after it's been in water
a couple of days... Hello!

27
00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:15.922
You know the best way to get revenge
on the mayor and his boys?

28
00:05:16.088 --> 00:05:19.258
You do exactly what we're doin'...
you protect the town.

29
00:05:24.347 --> 00:05:28.643
- Think you could go a little faster, pal?
- I'm goin' as fast as I can.

30
00:05:39.028 --> 00:05:41.030
Hey, wait!

31
00:05:42.657 --> 00:05:45.618
- Excuse me?
- You forgot to sign.

32
00:05:52.917 --> 00:05:54.919
Stay dry, now.

33
00:05:58.089 --> 00:06:00.091
Watch your back.

34
00:06:00.508 --> 00:06:02.718
For Christ's sake!

35
00:06:02.885 --> 00:06:06.764
Charlie, it's a flood.
You're gonna get a little wet. Take it easy.

36
00:06:06.931 --> 00:06:09.517
- Dispatch, this is 31.
- Go ahead, 31.

37
00:06:09.684 --> 00:06:12.520
We're leavin' Huntingburg.
We'll be back in an hour.

38
00:06:12.687 --> 00:06:16.357
- Ten-four. Get outta there.
- We're gone. Over and out.

39
00:06:19.819 --> 00:06:21.112
What?

40
00:06:22.113 --> 00:06:24.782
- Your ear.
- What about my ear?

41
00:06:24.949 --> 00:06:28.411
- You got major hair growth in there.
- Shut up.

42
00:06:28.577 --> 00:06:33.165
I'm serious. Somebody should get in there
with a weed whacker, clean that mess up.

43
00:06:33.332 --> 00:06:35.334
Here.

44
00:06:35.501 --> 00:06:40.047
You're givin' me one of your doughnuts? I
don't know what to say. I'm gettin' misty.

45
00:06:40.214 --> 00:06:42.466
Shut your mouth and you can have 'em all.

46
00:06:42.633 --> 00:06:45.886
I start eatin' these,
I'll never get out of this truck.

47
00:06:46.053 --> 00:06:49.515
I just love how you think
you're better than all this.

48
00:06:49.682 --> 00:06:51.642
What's not to like, Charlie?

49
00:06:51.809 --> 00:06:56.397
The dashing polyester outfit
or the solid, three-figure income?

50
00:06:57.315 --> 00:07:00.568
I don't believe you!
You ungrateful little shit.

51
00:07:00.735 --> 00:07:02.695
Relax. I was kidding.

52
00:07:02.862 --> 00:07:06.324
So that's all you think I've done, huh?
Just wasted my life away.

53
00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:09.160
- I didn't say that.
- Yeah, yeah.

54
00:07:09.327 --> 00:07:12.955
Buildin' a home, raisin' a family...

55
00:07:13.122 --> 00:07:16.083
- That's just stupid.
- I didn't say that either.

56
00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:19.962
You know what, Tom?
I don't give a rat's ass what you say.

57
00:07:36.312 --> 00:07:38.481
"Thus saith the Lord: 'Behold,...

58
00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:43.235
..waters shall rise up out of the north
and be an overflowing flood,...

59
00:07:43.402 --> 00:07:46.155
..and all the inhabitants
of the land shall howl."'

60
00:07:46.322 --> 00:07:49.366
Yes, sir. Jeremiah, Chapter 47, Verse 2.

61
00:07:49.533 --> 00:07:53.162
You're gonna be able to afford
a hell of a lot of Bibles, Ray.

62
00:07:53.329 --> 00:07:57.541
Me? First thing I'm gonna do
is to get my brother a lawyer,...

63
00:07:57.708 --> 00:07:59.752
..the best that money can buy.

64
00:07:59.919 --> 00:08:02.588
- What's he facin'?
- Thirty in.

65
00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:07.593
- He must've capped a cop or somethin'.
- No. Security guard, in the commission.

66
00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:10.471
He's got some piece of shit PD...

67
00:08:10.638 --> 00:08:12.306
Kenny.

68
00:08:12.473 --> 00:08:14.809
Kenny, take a look at 26 across.

69
00:08:17.603 --> 00:08:20.314
- Shit, Jim. I don't do crosswords.
- Just look at it.

70
00:08:20.481 --> 00:08:24.735
- Let me take a look at it.
- Never mind, Mr Mehlor. Kenny can read.

71
00:08:25.319 --> 00:08:27.321
26 across.

72
00:08:29.949 --> 00:08:32.368
"Mention money again and I'll..."

73
00:08:40.084 --> 00:08:42.044
Did I get it right?

74
00:08:43.295 --> 00:08:45.131
Yeah, Jim, you got it right.

75
00:08:47.133 --> 00:08:49.343
What a dope.

76
00:09:06.861 --> 00:09:09.405
- Jerk.
- Jackass.

77
00:09:11.407 --> 00:09:16.120
- Come on. Give us a kiss, huh?
- Get outta here! Get out, ya...

78
00:09:18.038 --> 00:09:21.959
- You really are a touchy old fart.
- I'm sorry.

79
00:09:22.126 --> 00:09:26.422
What was that about? I'm sittin' there
and all of a sudden you go postal on me.

80
00:09:26.589 --> 00:09:28.757
I dunno. I...

81
00:09:28.924 --> 00:09:31.010
It's just this weather.

82
00:09:31.177 --> 00:09:33.596
I just wanna get back.

83
00:09:35.222 --> 00:09:38.309
I do appreciate what you've done for me.
This is a good job.

84
00:09:38.475 --> 00:09:41.270
No, it's not. It stinks.

85
00:09:41.437 --> 00:09:44.815
Puttin' your ass on the line
for somebody else's money.

86
00:09:53.657 --> 00:09:57.995
- Where the hell's the road?
- It's there... somewhere.

87
00:10:01.248 --> 00:10:03.792
Look, Tom, I don't care
what you end up doing.

88
00:10:03.959 --> 00:10:05.419
Aw, Jesus, here we go.

89
00:10:05.586 --> 00:10:09.590
I just think that, whatever you do,
it's time you did some heavy lifting.

90
00:10:09.757 --> 00:10:11.425
- Stop.
- No, you gotta hear this.

91
00:10:11.592 --> 00:10:14.678
- Stop the truck. We're goin' downhill!
- Oh, Jesus!

92
00:10:25.856 --> 00:10:27.858
Wow!

93
00:10:32.571 --> 00:10:34.573
All right, back up.

94
00:10:37.493 --> 00:10:38.953
Slow, slow, slow.

95
00:10:54.969 --> 00:10:56.971
Goddamn it!

96
00:10:59.181 --> 00:11:02.643
- There's a dip in the road up there.
- I knew this would happen.

97
00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:06.897
I'll go see if there's anybody around
to give us a lift.

98
00:11:07.856 --> 00:11:10.859
Dispatch? Dispatch, this is 31.

99
00:11:11.026 --> 00:11:13.028
31 calling Dispatch.

100
00:11:13.779 --> 00:11:16.115
We're stuck outside of Huntingburg.

101
00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:25.249
Right by a sign...

102
00:11:26.709 --> 00:11:29.545
..saying "Welcome to Huntingburg".

103
00:11:33.340 --> 00:11:36.302
The town's been evacuated.
We won't get help from there.

104
00:11:36.468 --> 00:11:38.470
Dispatch can't get anyone out.

105
00:11:38.637 --> 00:11:41.473
They are aware we're carrying
a shitload of money?

106
00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:43.726
They called the National Guard.

107
00:11:43.892 --> 00:11:47.396
- They'll be here in a couple of hours.
- Couple of hours?

108
00:11:50.816 --> 00:11:51.775
Shit.

109
00:12:06.957 --> 00:12:08.584
Henry...

110
00:12:08.751 --> 00:12:12.546
I saw ya. Come on out.

111
00:12:14.048 --> 00:12:17.843
Henry! I'm not leavin'
till you come out.

112
00:12:19.928 --> 00:12:21.930
He's not comin' out.

113
00:12:23.474 --> 00:12:27.644
Henry, close the door. Don't go
out there, Henry. Get back in here.

114
00:12:27.811 --> 00:12:30.189
Why are you two still here?
Need some help?

115
00:12:30.356 --> 00:12:33.025
- No, we're just...
- We're setting traps.

116
00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:36.070
That's illegal, Doreen.

117
00:12:38.822 --> 00:12:40.991
You gonna arrest us, Sheriff?

118
00:12:41.533 --> 00:12:46.288
Hell, are you even sheriff any more,
Sheriff? Didn't you lose an election?

119
00:12:46.538 --> 00:12:48.540
I sure as hell know
I didn't vote for you.

120
00:12:48.707 --> 00:12:50.918
- Neither did Henry.
- Doreen!

121
00:12:51.085 --> 00:12:53.837
Look, you don't need to set traps.

122
00:12:54.004 --> 00:12:57.883
That's what they said in '73.
What the bastards didn't steal,...

123
00:12:58.050 --> 00:12:59.968
..they broke, just for the hell of it.

124
00:13:00.135 --> 00:13:01.970
That's not happening this time.

125
00:13:02.137 --> 00:13:05.307
- Damn right it's not!
- Look, you can't stay.

126
00:13:05.557 --> 00:13:08.143
- We're goin' to my sister's now.
- Good.

127
00:13:08.310 --> 00:13:11.105
As soon as we finish
setting the traps.

128
00:13:12.439 --> 00:13:17.486
Well, I'm sure glad one of us
has a backbone. Leave it up to you and...

129
00:13:17.653 --> 00:13:21.782
God'll understand if you have to drown her
in the basement, Henry.

130
00:13:25.953 --> 00:13:28.747
- We gotta get outta here.
- What about the money?

131
00:13:28.914 --> 00:13:32.376
The money's safe, we're not.
The water rose a foot in 20 minutes.

132
00:13:32.543 --> 00:13:36.380
The National Guard won't be here
any time soon. You do the math.

133
00:14:07.578 --> 00:14:09.580
Hello!

134
00:14:13.333 --> 00:14:16.378
- Hello!
- Hello!

135
00:14:17.463 --> 00:14:21.550
- You all right? Are you stuck?
- Yeah!

136
00:14:21.717 --> 00:14:26.138
OK! We're gonna try and help you get out.
All right?

137
00:14:28.015 --> 00:14:30.726
Looks like we're gonna
get outta here.

138
00:14:32.144 --> 00:14:35.689
- Why'd they do that?
- Uh... Probably just to see us better.

139
00:14:36.231 --> 00:14:38.734
So we can't see at all.

140
00:14:40.235 --> 00:14:44.698
Now listen up. This is my retirement fund.
Don't anybody screw it up.

141
00:14:46.074 --> 00:14:48.368
You hear me, Kenny? Kenny!

142
00:14:48.535 --> 00:14:50.996
- Get your head outta your ass.
- Yup.

143
00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:54.958
Only Dispatch and the National Guard
know we're here.

144
00:14:55.125 --> 00:15:00.005
Come on. Anybody with a scanner from
RadioShack could've picked up our signal.

145
00:15:00.255 --> 00:15:03.926
- Could you turn down those lights?
- Yeah! We'll bring you some rope!

146
00:15:04.092 --> 00:15:06.929
We're goin' blind!
Turn down those lights!

147
00:15:07.095 --> 00:15:10.557
- We're coming right over!
- Turn down your lights!

148
00:15:10.724 --> 00:15:12.184
Tom! Take it easy!

149
00:15:12.351 --> 00:15:13.310
Jim? Jim?

150
00:15:13.477 --> 00:15:15.312
Get in the truck, Charlie.

151
00:15:18.357 --> 00:15:20.609
- Kenny, what are you doin'?!
- Oh, shit!

152
00:15:22.236 --> 00:15:24.821
- What did I tell you?
- He went for his gun!

153
00:15:25.072 --> 00:15:26.949
Stop shooting!

154
00:15:28.075 --> 00:15:30.077
Stop shooting!

155
00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:34.623
Stop shooting!

156
00:15:39.586 --> 00:15:41.588
Charlie!

157
00:15:43.090 --> 00:15:45.092
Goddammit, Kenny!

158
00:15:45.259 --> 00:15:47.261
Goddammit!

159
00:15:49.972 --> 00:15:51.473
Hey!

160
00:15:52.474 --> 00:15:54.476
Everybody all right down there?

161
00:15:58.689 --> 00:16:00.232
Charlie...

162
00:16:01.149 --> 00:16:04.194
Sorry, Tom.

163
00:16:04.736 --> 00:16:07.864
Jesus. Oh, God.

164
00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:10.909
Damn. Damn!

165
00:16:19.877 --> 00:16:21.545
Hey!

166
00:16:23.088 --> 00:16:26.174
Look, we just want the money!

167
00:16:27.634 --> 00:16:29.386
You guys...

168
00:16:29.553 --> 00:16:31.555
You guys walk away!

169
00:16:31.722 --> 00:16:35.225
We won't kill ya! OK? How's that?

170
00:16:37.644 --> 00:16:40.063
You got 30 seconds!

171
00:16:42.190 --> 00:16:44.192
Walk away!

172
00:16:46.945 --> 00:16:51.658
Come on, guys, the clock is tickin'!
What's it gonna be?

173
00:16:58.415 --> 00:16:59.958
Shit.

174
00:17:50.717 --> 00:17:52.844
Son of a bitch. Ray...

175
00:18:01.978 --> 00:18:04.272
Your father would be real proud, Kenny.

176
00:18:04.439 --> 00:18:06.775
- He was goin' for his gun!
- Shut up.

177
00:18:07.859 --> 00:18:11.947
Mr Mehlor, I think we're gonna need
your science project.

178
00:18:12.114 --> 00:18:14.992
You teach your students
how to make things like that?

179
00:18:15.158 --> 00:18:18.954
Been in a high school lately? My students
taught me how to make them.

180
00:18:19.121 --> 00:18:21.123
Come on, come on.

181
00:18:36.722 --> 00:18:39.391
I'll be damned! Damn!

182
00:18:50.777 --> 00:18:52.779
Now, why would he do that?

183
00:18:53.739 --> 00:18:56.867
- He's tryin' to stay alive.
- What?

184
00:18:57.034 --> 00:19:00.579
Figures as long as we don't know
where the money is, we won't kill him.

185
00:19:00.746 --> 00:19:02.914
There could be another possibility.

186
00:19:03.081 --> 00:19:06.793
He could be thinkin' about
keepin' that money for himself.

187
00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:13.508
That is a possibility. Either way,
we're dealing with a slippery one.

188
00:19:13.675 --> 00:19:16.678
Jim, what are we gonna do now?

189
00:19:16.845 --> 00:19:20.348
Pretty soon this water will be
too deep for him to run in.

190
00:19:21.183 --> 00:19:23.977
But it'll be just deep enough for us.

191
00:19:53.673 --> 00:19:55.300
Mr Mehlor.

192
00:20:03.266 --> 00:20:05.268
Whoo-hoo!

193
00:20:09.314 --> 00:20:11.817
We should take a car too, huh?

194
00:20:13.443 --> 00:20:17.072
Hey, Jim, what about
this big bad boy here, huh?

195
00:20:17.239 --> 00:20:19.783
- It's got a big canopy.
- Nah, this is all we need.

196
00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:23.078
We're stealin', Jim.
Can't we just take anything we want?

197
00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:27.165
Water's not very deep yet. We need
something with a shallow draught.

198
00:20:27.332 --> 00:20:30.127
Mr Mehlor, find us some gas.

199
00:20:31.086 --> 00:20:33.088
Oh. Jim. Jim!

200
00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:41.805
Whooo-hoo!

201
00:21:21.678 --> 00:21:23.680
There he is!

202
00:21:56.129 --> 00:21:57.797
Jim!

203
00:21:57.964 --> 00:22:00.050
Jim, over here!

204
00:22:01.301 --> 00:22:03.595
The window. The window's broken.

205
00:22:03.762 --> 00:22:05.597
Let's get in and get him out.

206
00:22:05.764 --> 00:22:08.850
But whatever you do,
don't shoot him!

207
00:22:09.017 --> 00:22:11.478
Not till we find out
where that money is!

208
00:22:34.876 --> 00:22:37.003
Did you see that?!

209
00:22:57.274 --> 00:22:58.441
Where'd you go?

210
00:23:00.527 --> 00:23:02.070
Where'd you go?

211
00:23:04.114 --> 00:23:05.448
Hey!

212
00:23:09.035 --> 00:23:10.996
Come back here!

213
00:23:34.519 --> 00:23:36.938
- Ramming speed!
- Watch your step.

214
00:23:37.564 --> 00:23:39.065
Aargh!

215
00:23:47.907 --> 00:23:49.284
Low tide, sailor.

216
00:24:00.378 --> 00:24:01.963
Yo! You see him?

217
00:24:02.130 --> 00:24:04.799
- What the...? He's over here!
- Shit.

218
00:24:04.924 --> 00:24:07.343
Hey, Jim! Jim!

219
00:24:08.344 --> 00:24:11.014
He's over this way!

220
00:24:50.136 --> 00:24:53.098
Yeaaaaah!

221
00:25:03.358 --> 00:25:05.151
Damn.

222
00:25:41.187 --> 00:25:43.273
Shit.

223
00:25:50.572 --> 00:25:52.490
Nice driving, butt-wipe!

224
00:25:52.657 --> 00:25:55.493
- Serves you right for takin' my jacket!
- Get off me, man!

225
00:25:55.660 --> 00:26:00.331
I'm glad you're enjoyin' yourself. But
if he's dead how do we find the money?

226
00:26:00.498 --> 00:26:02.500
Oh, I wouldn't worry.

227
00:26:06.463 --> 00:26:08.590
He's still alive.

228
00:26:17.390 --> 00:26:21.352
Ray, I'm gonna need
a little inspiration, son.

229
00:26:24.189 --> 00:26:27.567
"With the raging flood, He makes an end
of those who oppose Him...

230
00:26:27.734 --> 00:26:30.737
..and He pursues His enemies
into darkness."

231
00:26:32.155 --> 00:26:36.159
- That's from a more obscure...
- I don't mean to interrupt Bible study,...

232
00:26:36.326 --> 00:26:39.287
..but has anybody realised
how screwed we are?

233
00:26:40.205 --> 00:26:44.876
We should be back in the motel room
right now, countin' our money... Argh!

234
00:26:46.961 --> 00:26:50.173
Nobody likes this particular
turn of events, Kenny.

235
00:26:50.340 --> 00:26:54.135
But we have a choice.
We can deal with it or we can walk away.

236
00:26:54.302 --> 00:26:57.138
It's a lot of money,
so I choose to deal with it.

237
00:26:57.305 --> 00:26:59.432
You wanna go? Fine. Start swimming.

238
00:26:59.599 --> 00:27:01.601
You wanna stay? That's fine too.

239
00:27:01.768 --> 00:27:04.062
But stop your goddamn whining!

240
00:27:06.523 --> 00:27:08.525
Loser.

241
00:28:20.263 --> 00:28:23.308
- Why are you here?
- I was setting the pumps.

242
00:28:23.474 --> 00:28:28.479
- I don't get what you see in that church.
- I don't expect you to, Wayne.

243
00:28:28.646 --> 00:28:32.650
Karen, did you think the order was
for everyone but you to evacuate?

244
00:28:32.817 --> 00:28:35.528
No. I was gonna go
as soon as I filled the pumps.

245
00:28:35.695 --> 00:28:39.115
But the next thing I know,
I got a looter on my hands and...

246
00:28:39.282 --> 00:28:44.621
Maybe I'm crazy, but I was expecting
a little... I don't know... gratitude?

247
00:28:44.746 --> 00:28:49.625
- I think it's great, what you did, Karen.
- That'll get you into her pants, Phil.

248
00:28:49.792 --> 00:28:52.086
That's not what I meant, Wayne.

249
00:28:52.253 --> 00:28:54.255
All right, all right!

250
00:28:54.839 --> 00:28:56.799
OK?

251
00:28:57.800 --> 00:29:01.304
What if he'd had a gun, Karen?
A lot of looters carry guns.

252
00:29:01.471 --> 00:29:03.681
I'm not a looter.

253
00:29:06.934 --> 00:29:10.271
- Jim, he may not even be in this school.
- Keep lookin'.

254
00:29:10.438 --> 00:29:12.440
You're wasting ammo. Use this.

255
00:29:12.607 --> 00:29:15.651
Kenny! If you're not dead, get up and help.

256
00:29:19.489 --> 00:29:22.158
God... dammit!

257
00:29:32.293 --> 00:29:35.421
- Why were you at the church?
- I told you. He was looting it.

258
00:29:35.588 --> 00:29:37.715
I just said I'm not a looter.

259
00:29:37.882 --> 00:29:40.635
You're the one who nailed me,
aren't you?

260
00:29:41.552 --> 00:29:44.972
- What the helI'd you hit me with?
- It was a crucifix.

261
00:29:46.015 --> 00:29:48.726
What? That was all that was there.

262
00:29:48.893 --> 00:29:53.064
Great. People will come around the world
to see the face of Jesus on my forehead.

263
00:29:53.231 --> 00:29:57.693
- Son, what were you doin' in the church?
- I was looking for a place to hide.

264
00:29:57.860 --> 00:30:00.905
From what? Swamp Thing?

265
00:30:01.656 --> 00:30:04.242
From the guys who killed my partner.

266
00:30:09.789 --> 00:30:14.293
I work for Armoured Transports. They
must've picked up our call to Dispatch.

267
00:30:14.460 --> 00:30:17.839
They knew exactly where we were.
Then all hell broke loose.

268
00:30:18.005 --> 00:30:21.592
- How much money did you have?
- A little over three million.

269
00:30:22.927 --> 00:30:26.222
The bank had us cleaning out branches
up and down the river.

270
00:30:26.389 --> 00:30:30.143
- They stole three million dollars?
- No, I don't think so.

271
00:30:31.102 --> 00:30:33.312
You took the money, didn't you?

272
00:30:33.855 --> 00:30:38.484
Yeah, I hid it in the cemetery. Tied it
to a crypt for some guy named... Portman.

273
00:30:38.651 --> 00:30:42.738
- What the helI'd you do that for?
- I don't like to carry that much cash.

274
00:30:43.156 --> 00:30:46.868
Wayne, use your head for something
besides wearing your hat.

275
00:30:47.034 --> 00:30:50.413
If he hadn't hid the money,
they'd have killed him too.

276
00:30:52.039 --> 00:30:53.833
Get out two shotguns and a rifle.

277
00:30:54.000 --> 00:30:57.587
- You got any ID?
- Uh, no. I left it in the truck.

278
00:30:57.754 --> 00:30:59.756
Colour me surprised

279
00:31:01.299 --> 00:31:05.344
- Do you believe him?
- Well, yes, Wayne, I do.

280
00:31:06.554 --> 00:31:08.473
And even if I didn't,...

281
00:31:08.639 --> 00:31:13.478
..I'd say we sure as hell have an obligation
to check it out. Don't you think?

282
00:31:14.479 --> 00:31:18.566
- I'll go with you, show you where it is.
- I think you'd better stay put.

283
00:31:18.733 --> 00:31:20.526
- That was a smart move...
- Yeah.

284
00:31:20.693 --> 00:31:23.488
We don't need
no armoured-car guy's help. Ow!

285
00:31:23.654 --> 00:31:27.450
Wayne, what's the worst thing
that's ever happened to you on this job?

286
00:31:27.617 --> 00:31:30.411
When old Mrs Dugan went after you
with a paint scraper?

287
00:31:30.578 --> 00:31:32.830
This man just got shot at.

288
00:31:32.997 --> 00:31:35.374
Phil, Wayne and I
will check out the cemetery.

289
00:31:35.541 --> 00:31:39.712
Escort Slugger here out of town. Get her
to some high ground, then come on back.

290
00:31:39.879 --> 00:31:41.797
Uh...

291
00:31:41.964 --> 00:31:45.426
Um... I really have to
fill those pumps.

292
00:31:45.635 --> 00:31:48.095
Not any more you don't.

293
00:31:49.931 --> 00:31:51.641
Wayne...

294
00:31:51.807 --> 00:31:53.809
He could still be lyin'.

295
00:31:58.523 --> 00:32:02.318
Sheriff, they killed my partner
without any warning.

296
00:32:02.777 --> 00:32:05.488
And they're gonna regret that.

297
00:32:07.907 --> 00:32:11.410
- Phil, you take Karen in her boat.
- You got it, Sheriff.

298
00:32:27.885 --> 00:32:31.222
You can do it, Phil. The men
of Huntingburg are countin' on ya!

299
00:32:32.682 --> 00:32:35.601
Bite me, Wayne.

300
00:32:54.537 --> 00:32:56.497
Just perfect

301
00:32:59.917 --> 00:33:04.171
Phil, I don't know if you noticed
those stained-glass windows,...

302
00:33:04.463 --> 00:33:07.800
..but do you know how much work
I've put into them? Do you know?

303
00:33:08.384 --> 00:33:11.178
Please! It'll take five minutes
to fill those pumps!

304
00:33:11.429 --> 00:33:14.724
Look, Karen. You know I'd do
just about anything for you.

305
00:33:14.891 --> 00:33:19.895
But the sheriff told me to take you outta
town. I'm sorry. It's for your own good.

306
00:33:21.772 --> 00:33:24.942
- What are you doing?
- If you won't take me, I'll have to swim.

307
00:33:25.109 --> 00:33:29.488
- Nobody's swimming. Karen, sit down.
- Wait a minute. This is my boat.

308
00:33:32.783 --> 00:33:35.077
You swim!

309
00:33:35.244 --> 00:33:37.246
Karen!

310
00:33:44.295 --> 00:33:46.047
Shit!

311
00:33:46.213 --> 00:33:48.883
Goddammit! Come on!

312
00:34:02.605 --> 00:34:03.564
Sheriff, come in.

313
00:34:08.110 --> 00:34:10.446
Sheriff, a lot of water
is comin' your way!

314
00:34:41.227 --> 00:34:43.229
Oh... God!

315
00:34:51.445 --> 00:34:53.447
Hey! Look out!

316
00:35:15.928 --> 00:35:17.930
Oh, no!

317
00:35:19.432 --> 00:35:20.891
Help!

318
00:35:52.506 --> 00:35:54.759
Jesus.

319
00:35:57.052 --> 00:35:59.263
Hang on, Ray.

320
00:36:01.140 --> 00:36:05.227
Kenny! Get that jet ski!

321
00:36:58.155 --> 00:37:01.367
Come on. Come on. Come on, come on!

322
00:37:04.829 --> 00:37:06.956
Oh, yeah.

323
00:37:30.646 --> 00:37:32.231
Perfect. I can drive outta here.

324
00:38:05.681 --> 00:38:08.100
Wayne, you locked him in.

325
00:40:16.937 --> 00:40:18.439
Come here!

326
00:40:24.987 --> 00:40:28.449
- Are you OK?
- Yeah, never better.

327
00:40:31.910 --> 00:40:34.371
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

328
00:40:35.622 --> 00:40:38.333
- What happened?
- I don't know.

329
00:40:39.835 --> 00:40:43.422
- Another levee must have broken.
- Ah. Great.

330
00:40:44.715 --> 00:40:46.717
Let's get outta here.

331
00:40:56.060 --> 00:40:57.978
It's them. Let's go!

332
00:40:58.645 --> 00:41:01.231
Kenny! Go that way!

333
00:41:01.732 --> 00:41:03.525
All right!

334
00:41:09.782 --> 00:41:11.784
Whoo-hoo!

335
00:41:22.211 --> 00:41:24.213
Come on!

336
00:41:35.933 --> 00:41:38.060
I'm gonna get your little punk ass!

337
00:41:38.227 --> 00:41:40.312
Come on! Where are you?

338
00:41:43.649 --> 00:41:44.775
Whooh!

339
00:41:45.067 --> 00:41:47.778
- Tell them where the money is.
- I can't.

340
00:41:47.945 --> 00:41:50.781
- Well, I can!
- Listen to me. Listen!

341
00:41:55.577 --> 00:41:57.621
If they know where it is, they'll kill us.

342
00:41:57.788 --> 00:41:59.790
- Whooh!
- Down!

343
00:42:04.628 --> 00:42:06.630
Yee-ha!

344
00:42:14.012 --> 00:42:20.144
- So what do we do now?
- Just drive around till we run outta gas?

345
00:42:20.310 --> 00:42:23.647
I spent months restoring that church.
I left it to save your ass.

346
00:42:23.814 --> 00:42:25.816
So spare me, OK?

347
00:42:26.775 --> 00:42:28.986
All right.

348
00:42:29.153 --> 00:42:32.281
We'll go down here
till we find a place for you to lay low.

349
00:42:32.447 --> 00:42:37.661
I'll go back to the truck and wait for the
National Guard. They should be here soon.

350
00:42:39.580 --> 00:42:41.915
- You all right?
- Yeah, I'm fine.

351
00:42:42.082 --> 00:42:44.168
I think the heater just kicked in.

352
00:42:49.423 --> 00:42:54.553
- At least we're out of the rain, right?
- Oh, yeah. This is real cosy.

353
00:43:03.061 --> 00:43:05.272
Is he dead?

354
00:43:07.941 --> 00:43:12.404
- Is he dead?
- No. Somebody must've gotten him out.

355
00:43:13.405 --> 00:43:16.074
- Who?
- I dunno.

356
00:43:17.034 --> 00:43:19.036
- Maybe Karen?
- Karen?

357
00:43:19.953 --> 00:43:22.789
How the hell could she have?
You took her outta town.

358
00:43:22.956 --> 00:43:26.460
- Well, yeah, I...
- Let's hear it, Phil.

359
00:43:28.295 --> 00:43:31.173
Well, it happened real fast. OK?

360
00:43:35.093 --> 00:43:37.179
Have you ever been robbed before?

361
00:43:37.346 --> 00:43:40.224
No. I've only been doin' this
a couple of months.

362
00:43:40.390 --> 00:43:41.934
Oh.

363
00:43:42.100 --> 00:43:44.102
Yeah, I used to... uh...

364
00:43:45.020 --> 00:43:47.105
..sell construction machinery.

365
00:43:48.190 --> 00:43:53.320
I was doin' all right. It just, uh...
didn't really seem right any more.

366
00:43:54.238 --> 00:43:56.114
So how'd you end up doin' this?

367
00:43:56.281 --> 00:43:58.784
My Uncle Charlie did me a favour
and got me in.

368
00:43:58.951 --> 00:44:00.953
Nice favour

369
00:44:01.536 --> 00:44:03.789
So what's he gonna say after tonight?

370
00:44:05.457 --> 00:44:07.876
He was my partner in the truck.

371
00:44:08.418 --> 00:44:10.420
Oh.

372
00:44:10.587 --> 00:44:12.506
Sorry.

373
00:44:12.673 --> 00:44:14.800
Yeah.

374
00:44:14.967 --> 00:44:17.719
Does she know karate or something, Phil?

375
00:44:18.804 --> 00:44:21.014
Maybe kung fu!

376
00:44:21.181 --> 00:44:24.851
I just can't see how else
she could overpower the likes of you.

377
00:44:25.018 --> 00:44:27.604
- Just shut up, Wayne.
- Shut up, both of you.

378
00:44:27.771 --> 00:44:31.066
Let's go find Karen
and see if she's got him.

379
00:44:37.948 --> 00:44:40.325
I wonder whose car this is.

380
00:44:40.576 --> 00:44:45.247
Whoever it is,
they like Pat Benatar, Eddie Money and...

381
00:44:45.414 --> 00:44:47.541
Oh. The soundtrack to Footloose.

382
00:44:47.708 --> 00:44:49.459
Really?

383
00:44:49.626 --> 00:44:52.462
Oh, my God.
This is my car from high school.

384
00:44:58.719 --> 00:45:01.305
Maybe we should get outta here, huh?

385
00:45:33.670 --> 00:45:35.881
Get your feet out of the water.

386
00:45:41.637 --> 00:45:43.639
Whoo!

387
00:45:46.475 --> 00:45:49.186
- Oh, shit. This thing's metal.
- Oh, God.

388
00:45:49.978 --> 00:45:51.980
Let's get off!

389
00:45:55.484 --> 00:45:57.361
- I got him!
- No!

390
00:46:00.947 --> 00:46:03.283
- I got him!
- Listen. We gotta get...

391
00:46:10.082 --> 00:46:12.000
Get out of the water!

392
00:46:23.887 --> 00:46:25.889
Come on, get out!

393
00:46:27.224 --> 00:46:29.393
Get out of the water!

394
00:46:30.018 --> 00:46:34.356
- The transformer's gonna blow!
- Hurry! It's gonna blow up!

395
00:46:40.779 --> 00:46:42.781
Hurry up! Come on over here!

396
00:46:43.740 --> 00:46:45.992
No, no, no! Over here!

397
00:46:46.159 --> 00:46:48.412
Get off of that thing! It's metal!

398
00:46:48.578 --> 00:46:50.497
Come on! Give me your hand!

399
00:46:50.664 --> 00:46:52.290
Give me your hand!

400
00:47:13.019 --> 00:47:15.147
Jim, down here.

401
00:47:15.313 --> 00:47:17.315
What the hell is goin' on?

402
00:47:33.582 --> 00:47:35.167
Oh!

403
00:47:43.300 --> 00:47:45.552
Careful. Watch your step.

404
00:47:45.719 --> 00:47:47.762
You so much as breathe funny...

405
00:47:47.929 --> 00:47:50.599
..and your head goes out that window
without you.

406
00:47:51.808 --> 00:47:54.227
Jim! Jesus... Kenny!

407
00:47:54.394 --> 00:47:56.438
Hold on. Jesus Christ!

408
00:47:56.605 --> 00:47:58.315
Kenny!

409
00:47:58.482 --> 00:47:59.983
Jim! Kenny.

410
00:48:02.652 --> 00:48:06.031
- Come on, Kenny.
- Jesus Christ!

411
00:48:06.198 --> 00:48:09.784
Now put your hands up real slow.

412
00:48:09.951 --> 00:48:12.204
Like you were in a big jar of molasses.

413
00:48:14.831 --> 00:48:18.585
- That's it.
- Doreen, haven't killed anybody, have ya?

414
00:48:18.752 --> 00:48:22.005
I've got everything under control, Henry.
Go back to sleep.

415
00:48:22.172 --> 00:48:24.508
Uh-uh-uh-uh!

416
00:48:25.759 --> 00:48:27.802
Jesus, Doreen!

417
00:48:28.178 --> 00:48:30.180
You caught a whole gang!

418
00:48:32.557 --> 00:48:35.393
Smells like somethin' died in there.

419
00:48:36.394 --> 00:48:38.605
- Well?
- They're not there.

420
00:48:39.648 --> 00:48:43.068
Where in the hell could they go?
They don't have a boat.

421
00:48:43.235 --> 00:48:45.904
I don't know.
And, frankly, I don't care.

422
00:48:49.783 --> 00:48:54.079
- It hurts.
- You're gonna be all right, Kenny.

423
00:48:54.829 --> 00:48:57.958
Mr Mehlor knows about these things
and he thinks so.

424
00:48:58.708 --> 00:49:03.296
Ain't that right, Mr Mehlor? Don't you
think Kenny's gonna be all right?

425
00:49:04.673 --> 00:49:07.676
Yeah. Yeah, Kenny,
you're gonna be just fine.

426
00:49:08.343 --> 00:49:11.471
I know that you...
you didn't want me to come, Jim.

427
00:49:11.638 --> 00:49:16.560
What are you talkin' about? We couldn't
have done anything without you.

428
00:49:21.064 --> 00:49:26.278
The pain... is goin' away.
The pain is goin' away. I'm OK.

429
00:49:26.444 --> 00:49:28.488
Ah. See? What did I tell ya?

430
00:49:35.996 --> 00:49:39.082
When you said
that I was gonna be all right,...

431
00:49:39.249 --> 00:49:41.251
..I thought you were shittin' me.

432
00:49:42.294 --> 00:49:46.089
I wouldn't shit you, kid.
I wouldn't shit you.

433
00:49:46.256 --> 00:49:48.925
See? You... just gotta...

434
00:49:49.050 --> 00:49:51.052
You just gotta...

435
00:49:54.139 --> 00:49:55.932
..trust me.

436
00:50:08.445 --> 00:50:10.822
Well, isn't that just wonderful

437
00:50:10.989 --> 00:50:13.783
Now those bastards
are gonna want to kill us too.

438
00:50:13.950 --> 00:50:17.412
- Why did you have to pick this house?
- We thought it was empty.

439
00:50:17.871 --> 00:50:20.540
You know what?
The house next door is empty.

440
00:50:20.665 --> 00:50:24.252
What do you say we go back downstairs
and you two keep moving?

441
00:50:24.586 --> 00:50:26.922
We're not sending them out to the wolves!

442
00:50:27.088 --> 00:50:31.134
Oh, we're not, are we? Well,
what's your plan, General Schwarzkopf

443
00:50:31.301 --> 00:50:33.553
- I just don't think...
- I have to go anyway.

444
00:50:33.720 --> 00:50:37.057
The National Guard will be
at the truck soon. I should meet them.

445
00:50:37.223 --> 00:50:39.225
- He can use our boat.
- Henry!

446
00:50:39.392 --> 00:50:43.772
- Well, he can't swim that far.
- Henry, they are not taking our boat!

447
00:50:43.938 --> 00:50:47.651
Oh, fine, then!
Why don't you give them the TV set too?

448
00:50:47.817 --> 00:50:50.153
And what about the china? Or our silver?

449
00:50:50.320 --> 00:50:53.031
- I'm Tom.
- Watch yourself, Tom.

450
00:50:53.198 --> 00:50:55.367
I don't wanna have to
save your life again.

451
00:50:55.533 --> 00:51:01.081
Henry! Don't you ignore me!
You get right back up here this min...

452
00:51:01.247 --> 00:51:02.248
Henry!

453
00:51:05.502 --> 00:51:07.253
Here you go.

454
00:51:15.637 --> 00:51:18.473
You give away our only boat
in the middle of a flood.

455
00:51:18.640 --> 00:51:22.435
You are a genius, Henry.
A regular Einstein!

456
00:51:22.602 --> 00:51:24.604
You wanna come with me?

457
00:51:26.189 --> 00:51:30.318
Jesus, Henry! What are you waiting for...
a kiss goodbye? Get in here!

458
00:51:31.736 --> 00:51:34.447
- Thanks.
- Look at my curtains!

459
00:51:34.614 --> 00:51:38.618
- Put that window down now!
- All right, all right.

460
00:51:43.164 --> 00:51:45.166
Pow! Pow!

461
00:51:47.502 --> 00:51:49.671
Why don't we just get him now?

462
00:51:49.838 --> 00:51:53.800
Nah. If our resourceful young friend
hears us comin',...

463
00:51:53.967 --> 00:51:56.720
..he'll electrocute us or sink us.

464
00:51:56.886 --> 00:51:59.347
Or one of you knot-heads will shoot him.

465
00:52:00.515 --> 00:52:02.600
Besides, I know where he's going.

466
00:52:04.310 --> 00:52:07.188
What I'd like to know
is where he came from.

467
00:52:36.384 --> 00:52:38.136
Agh! Ugh!

468
00:52:45.643 --> 00:52:48.521
Now, I know it's your job
to protect that money, son.

469
00:52:48.688 --> 00:52:53.318
But before you try anything tricky,
there's something I want you to see.

470
00:52:54.778 --> 00:52:55.737
Aw, shit.

471
00:52:55.904 --> 00:52:59.240
You may be foolish enough
to give your life to protect that money.

472
00:52:59.407 --> 00:53:02.702
The question is,
are you willing to give theirs?

473
00:53:02.869 --> 00:53:06.581
I'll show you where the money is,
but you gotta let them go.

474
00:53:07.165 --> 00:53:11.169
- Nah. It's better if we all stick together.
- That's the deal.

475
00:53:11.336 --> 00:53:14.672
You say all you want's the money.
Prove it. Let 'em go.

476
00:53:14.839 --> 00:53:17.884
We could be safe in our home
instead of out here in this boat...

477
00:53:18.051 --> 00:53:20.053
..with these lowlife scumbags!

478
00:53:28.937 --> 00:53:31.940
- Let 'em go.
- Thank you. Thank you.

479
00:53:32.190 --> 00:53:34.651
- Right this way, please.
- Out of the water.

480
00:53:56.464 --> 00:53:58.466
Watch your step.

481
00:53:59.717 --> 00:54:03.596
- How about Karen?
- In the attic. They never saw her.

482
00:54:22.240 --> 00:54:26.119
Faster, Henry! The bastards
might change their minds!

483
00:54:26.286 --> 00:54:30.165
Come on! Stop lily-dipping! Move it!

484
00:54:33.543 --> 00:54:35.253
What are you doing?

485
00:54:35.420 --> 00:54:39.090
I'm going to row back there
and see if he will shoot you.

486
00:54:39.424 --> 00:54:41.593
Or me. It's fine either way.

487
00:54:41.759 --> 00:54:42.760
Henry!

488
00:54:42.927 --> 00:54:46.139
- Do you want me to get us outta here?
- Yes, of course.

489
00:54:46.306 --> 00:54:48.725
Then shut the fuck up!

490
00:54:55.398 --> 00:54:57.317
Sheriff, there she is!

491
00:55:10.914 --> 00:55:14.626
- What the hell is goin' on?
- This happened in a flood in Georgia.

492
00:55:14.792 --> 00:55:17.378
The ground gets soggy.
The caskets are airtight.

493
00:55:17.545 --> 00:55:20.423
Anybody who hasn't been planted too long
just pops up.

494
00:55:20.590 --> 00:55:24.219
You teach your students stuff like that,
no wonder they kicked you out.

495
00:55:24.385 --> 00:55:25.970
All right, where is it?

496
00:55:26.137 --> 00:55:29.807
It's kinda hard to tell now
with the water so deep.

497
00:55:33.853 --> 00:55:36.856
All right, all right. It's over that way.

498
00:55:57.085 --> 00:55:59.462
They're not coming, son.

499
00:56:02.632 --> 00:56:07.845
- The National Guard. They're not coming.
- I don't know what you're talkin' about.

500
00:56:08.596 --> 00:56:14.102
I know you're stalling us, waiting for the
National Guard, but they're not coming.

501
00:56:14.268 --> 00:56:16.729
Did you intercept Charlie's call?
Call them off?

502
00:56:16.896 --> 00:56:20.233
Didn't have to call them off.
They never were coming.

503
00:56:21.901 --> 00:56:24.320
We didn't intercept Charlie's call.

504
00:56:24.696 --> 00:56:26.823
Charlie called us.

505
00:56:26.990 --> 00:56:28.658
What?

506
00:56:28.825 --> 00:56:31.911
Sheriff, I'd love to help you out,
but I can't leave.

507
00:56:32.078 --> 00:56:35.331
Water comes over the top again,
it's bye-bye dam, bye-bye town.

508
00:56:35.623 --> 00:56:38.167
Hell, I could use
a little help here myself.

509
00:56:38.334 --> 00:56:42.213
Hank! Remember when Jack Finch
was holed up in Mike Crane's barn...

510
00:56:42.380 --> 00:56:44.090
..and said he'd burn it down?

511
00:56:44.257 --> 00:56:46.926
Yeah! I got the dumb son of a bitch
to come out.

512
00:56:47.093 --> 00:56:51.347
Right. And before you went in,
I deputised you, you dumb son of a bitch.

513
00:56:51.514 --> 00:56:55.768
So this is not a request, it's an order:
you get down here now!

514
00:56:56.019 --> 00:56:58.229
- I won't need you for long.
- Yes, sir.

515
00:56:58.396 --> 00:57:00.398
Bring your gun.

516
00:57:01.232 --> 00:57:04.152
We were gonna hit you
just before you got to the interstate.

517
00:57:04.319 --> 00:57:08.406
- But you got stuck so we changed plan.
- Bullshit. This is bullshit!

518
00:57:10.199 --> 00:57:11.367
Bullshit!

519
00:57:11.534 --> 00:57:15.538
I knew Charlie from when we both worked
for the Johnstown Company.

520
00:57:15.705 --> 00:57:20.335
His parents
liked Charlie McCarthy on the radio.

521
00:57:20.501 --> 00:57:23.504
His wife Mary died a year ago
of a heart attack.

522
00:57:23.671 --> 00:57:26.215
He had a son and a daughter,
both grown with...

523
00:57:26.382 --> 00:57:31.429
Son of a bitch! That was the plan, huh?
Kill Charlie, keep his share of the money?

524
00:57:39.228 --> 00:57:41.230
That was an accident.

525
00:57:42.482 --> 00:57:46.152
Kenny killed Charlie cos he didn't know
Charlie was on my side.

526
00:57:46.819 --> 00:57:48.821
I never told him.

527
00:57:49.864 --> 00:57:52.867
Kenny liked to talk.
Shouldn't even have been there.

528
00:57:53.034 --> 00:57:57.955
But his father asked me to look after him.
Guess I didn't do too good a job of that.

529
00:57:58.122 --> 00:58:02.293
Excuse me, Jim! I hate to interrupt,
but can we just find the money...

530
00:58:02.460 --> 00:58:05.129
..and get the hell outta here?

531
00:58:06.672 --> 00:58:08.174
Right.

532
00:58:09.175 --> 00:58:12.887
All right. Now listen.
I'm gonna ask you one more time.

533
00:58:13.387 --> 00:58:16.724
And before you start
bullshittin' me again, think of this.

534
00:58:16.891 --> 00:58:18.851
I've had a very frustrating night.

535
00:58:19.602 --> 00:58:22.480
While I may not find the money
if I kill you,...

536
00:58:24.107 --> 00:58:27.568
..I'm at the point now
where I just don't care.

537
00:58:30.571 --> 00:58:35.618
All right, I'll tell you where it is but...
I don't think it's gonna do you much good.

538
00:58:45.294 --> 00:58:47.296
Go on, get it.

539
00:58:59.016 --> 00:59:03.479
"At night we'd go down to the river,
and into the river we'd dive."

540
00:59:05.982 --> 00:59:09.944
That's Springsteen, man. "The River."
I'm all out of Bible quotes.

541
00:59:20.288 --> 00:59:23.332
- Looks like somebody beat you to it.
- What?!

542
00:59:24.083 --> 00:59:25.960
Son of a bitch!

543
00:59:51.819 --> 00:59:54.113
Aaargh...

544
00:59:54.906 --> 00:59:57.742
Stop! You'll hit Tom!

545
00:59:59.160 --> 01:00:01.913
Hold your fire! Hold your fire!

546
01:00:25.228 --> 01:00:28.606
I know you'd like nothing better
than to shoot me!

547
01:00:28.773 --> 01:00:33.527
But, in order to do that, you're gonna
have to shoot through young Tom here!

548
01:00:43.663 --> 01:00:45.540
OK.

549
01:01:02.265 --> 01:01:04.100
Karen!

550
01:01:06.727 --> 01:01:08.271
Karen!

551
01:01:10.106 --> 01:01:13.651
That's who you thought
was comin' to rescue you?!

552
01:01:13.818 --> 01:01:15.152
Karen!

553
01:01:21.993 --> 01:01:23.703
Watch your head!

554
01:01:45.099 --> 01:01:47.977
Somebody mind tellin' me
what the hell's goin' on?

555
01:01:48.644 --> 01:01:51.314
Why, hello, Hank.

556
01:01:51.439 --> 01:01:55.234
You know that money I told you about
from the armoured truck?

557
01:01:56.068 --> 01:01:58.946
Well... we're gonna keep it.

558
01:02:01.115 --> 01:02:04.118
Three million dollars, four ways.

559
01:02:07.913 --> 01:02:10.875
750 apiece. You OK with that?

560
01:02:15.463 --> 01:02:16.922
Hank?

561
01:02:18.049 --> 01:02:21.677
- Are you OK with that?
- 750 thousand dollars?

562
01:02:23.554 --> 01:02:26.307
You damn straight I'm OK with that!

563
01:02:27.475 --> 01:02:29.310
I don't see what we need him for.

564
01:02:29.477 --> 01:02:32.355
I guess you ain't never
been huntin' with Hank.

565
01:02:34.774 --> 01:02:38.527
OK! We got two behind that crypt.
Go get 'em!

566
01:02:49.205 --> 01:02:51.707
Maybe I'm not OK with it.

567
01:02:56.170 --> 01:02:58.756
- Come on now, Phil.
- You're gonna kill people?

568
01:03:00.174 --> 01:03:05.554
They're looters, Phil. They come and steal
from an armoured truck in our town.

569
01:03:08.808 --> 01:03:11.936
What about Tom and Karen?
They're not looters.

570
01:03:12.103 --> 01:03:15.147
No... They're witnesses.

571
01:03:24.323 --> 01:03:25.866
Shit!

572
01:03:55.104 --> 01:03:57.148
Look at it.

573
01:04:00.651 --> 01:04:04.739
- Some of these bags will be yours, Phil.
- But you're the sheriff!

574
01:04:12.997 --> 01:04:14.999
Here.

575
01:04:19.128 --> 01:04:23.174
- For 20 years you've looked out for...
- For 20 years, I've eaten shit,...

576
01:04:23.340 --> 01:04:27.344
..breakfast, lunch and dinner!
Well, tonight I'm changin' the menu.

577
01:04:27.511 --> 01:04:30.681
From now on, everything I eat
is gonna be shit-free.

578
01:04:45.154 --> 01:04:49.867
Can I make it any clearer, Phil?
You want me to draw you a picture?

579
01:04:51.076 --> 01:04:53.788
- I can't let you do it.
- Oh, for...

580
01:04:57.249 --> 01:05:01.003
OK, Phil. Here's how it's gonna go.

581
01:05:01.170 --> 01:05:04.215
I'm gonna hear one of two things
come outta you.

582
01:05:04.381 --> 01:05:07.885
Either I'm gonna hear you say
that you're in with us,...

583
01:05:08.052 --> 01:05:12.139
..or I'm gonna hear a bullet
come outta that gun and go into me.

584
01:05:12.806 --> 01:05:19.146
750 thousand dollars, or you kill me.
Your choice.

585
01:05:27.154 --> 01:05:28.656
There we go.

586
01:05:43.671 --> 01:05:46.549
Tom! Grab the boat!

587
01:06:08.195 --> 01:06:10.114
Thanks.

588
01:06:12.449 --> 01:06:14.660
We're goin' too slow.

589
01:06:17.037 --> 01:06:18.831
Take the wheel.

590
01:06:22.251 --> 01:06:24.253
Whoa! Watch it!

591
01:06:27.464 --> 01:06:29.174
Come on! Come on!

592
01:07:43.332 --> 01:07:45.334
Come on!

593
01:07:47.461 --> 01:07:50.005
There you are!

594
01:07:52.132 --> 01:07:54.009
Whoa, boy! Where you goin', huh?

595
01:07:57.638 --> 01:07:59.640
Son of a bitch!

596
01:08:13.612 --> 01:08:16.115
Son of a bitch!
You're pissin' me off!

597
01:09:02.453 --> 01:09:04.705
- Does that hurt?
- Yeah.

598
01:09:04.872 --> 01:09:06.874
Good.

599
01:09:08.542 --> 01:09:11.295
Hank, go get some empty bottles.
We'll smoke 'em out.

600
01:09:11.462 --> 01:09:14.506
- You got it.
- Wait. What about the dam?

601
01:09:14.673 --> 01:09:18.719
- It'll be fine.
- If it goes, it'll wipe out the whole town.

602
01:09:20.262 --> 01:09:21.722
Screw the town.

603
01:09:23.599 --> 01:09:25.893
I'll probably get hepatitis or something.

604
01:09:26.059 --> 01:09:29.605
Hepatitis? Nah.
That's the least of your problems.

605
01:09:32.107 --> 01:09:34.568
- Where you going?
- There's a room back here.

606
01:09:34.735 --> 01:09:38.572
- I'll look for something to put on this.
- You been here before?

607
01:09:38.739 --> 01:09:40.741
Oh, yeah.

608
01:09:41.075 --> 01:09:43.076
I saw Jesus!

609
01:09:53.837 --> 01:09:56.256
Did Charlie have cancer or something?

610
01:09:57.049 --> 01:09:59.426
You mean, why did he get into this?

611
01:09:59.593 --> 01:10:01.970
No, no cancer.

612
01:10:02.763 --> 01:10:05.474
Didn't you ever think about
takin' the money?

613
01:10:05.641 --> 01:10:08.602
- No.
- No? Hah!

614
01:10:09.603 --> 01:10:13.190
- I'm happy to disappoint you.
- Yeah.

615
01:10:15.025 --> 01:10:18.070
- What are you gonna do with it?
- As little as possible.

616
01:10:20.656 --> 01:10:22.825
- Belize.
- What?

617
01:10:23.742 --> 01:10:27.663
Belize. It's a small country
in Central America on the Atlantic side.

618
01:10:27.955 --> 01:10:30.999
I know where Belize is.
What about it?

619
01:10:33.001 --> 01:10:35.921
They speak English,
dollar goes a long way,...

620
01:10:36.088 --> 01:10:38.549
..beautiful beaches, friendly people,...

621
01:10:38.799 --> 01:10:41.343
..liberal banking laws,...

622
01:10:41.510 --> 01:10:43.512
..very liberal banking laws.

623
01:10:44.388 --> 01:10:48.475
Nah. You never once
thought about takin' that money.

624
01:10:50.477 --> 01:10:53.647
You can't ride in that truck
and not think about it.

625
01:10:54.773 --> 01:10:57.484
Reckon that's how it started with Charlie.

626
01:11:26.096 --> 01:11:29.182
- What are you doin'?
- Too many bodies with bullets in 'em.

627
01:11:29.349 --> 01:11:32.352
I'll take her to her house,
make it look like she drowned.

628
01:11:32.519 --> 01:11:34.229
Don't you do it, Wayne!

629
01:11:34.396 --> 01:11:38.066
Saving her life might've
actually gotten you laid, Phil.

630
01:11:38.233 --> 01:11:40.110
Don't you touch her!

631
01:11:43.739 --> 01:11:45.532
Get back here!

632
01:11:45.699 --> 01:11:48.660
For Christ's sake,
just dump her here, Wayne!

633
01:11:48.827 --> 01:11:51.288
I'm gonna kill you, Bryce!

634
01:11:51.455 --> 01:11:53.749
Shit. Where the hell's he takin' her?

635
01:11:59.922 --> 01:12:04.593
Where do you think you're going?
You won't help matters by gettin' shot.

636
01:12:04.760 --> 01:12:08.555
- They're gone. You don't know where.
- The sheriff knows. I'll ask him.

637
01:12:08.722 --> 01:12:11.308
You'd be dead
before you cross the sandbags.

638
01:12:11.475 --> 01:12:13.727
They'll come for us.
Ask 'em when they get here.

639
01:12:13.894 --> 01:12:16.897
- What if they don't come?
- I wouldn't worry about that.

640
01:12:28.992 --> 01:12:30.994
Whoo!

641
01:12:41.088 --> 01:12:42.047
Sorry, Karen.

642
01:12:55.018 --> 01:12:57.020
Wayne.

643
01:12:58.021 --> 01:13:00.482
Wayne, what are you doing?

644
01:13:02.776 --> 01:13:07.030
"Dear Penthouse,
I always thought your letters were fake...

645
01:13:07.531 --> 01:13:09.741
..until the wildest thing happened to me."

646
01:13:14.162 --> 01:13:15.330
Jesus.

647
01:13:15.706 --> 01:13:18.500
- They're not comin' out.
- Fire's not catchin'.

648
01:13:18.667 --> 01:13:20.669
We gotta get 'em outta there.

649
01:13:25.757 --> 01:13:31.346
"Her name was Karen, and ever since
she come back from college,...

650
01:13:31.513 --> 01:13:35.183
..she made it clear
that she was too good for us local folk."

651
01:13:35.350 --> 01:13:37.352
"Now here she was in handcuffs."

652
01:13:37.519 --> 01:13:41.732
"I said 'What the heck
is goin' on here, ma'am?"'

653
01:13:42.774 --> 01:13:44.776
"And she said..."

654
01:13:48.739 --> 01:13:51.325
- "And she said..."
- Get off, you psycho!

655
01:13:52.034 --> 01:13:54.411
You really think I'll play your sick game?

656
01:13:54.578 --> 01:13:56.455
Why not?

657
01:14:03.086 --> 01:14:05.380
Well, that won't do.

658
01:14:05.547 --> 01:14:07.632
You'll, uh... excuse me?

659
01:14:10.969 --> 01:14:12.971
You wait right there, now.

660
01:14:32.741 --> 01:14:35.577
Well, I got the candle.

661
01:14:38.955 --> 01:14:41.666
Mood lighting.

662
01:14:43.460 --> 01:14:45.629
"It was cold and rainy that night."

663
01:14:46.505 --> 01:14:50.217
"All I really wanted was
to get someplace warm and dry."

664
01:14:54.054 --> 01:14:56.264
Are you in the mood yet?

665
01:14:59.101 --> 01:15:00.268
No.

666
01:16:13.341 --> 01:16:15.343
Oh, my God!

667
01:16:20.390 --> 01:16:22.017
No!

668
01:16:22.434 --> 01:16:24.019
No!

669
01:16:24.394 --> 01:16:25.687
Oh...

670
01:16:25.854 --> 01:16:27.606
Come on... Come on!

671
01:17:07.103 --> 01:17:09.397
Phil! Cover that side!

672
01:17:40.637 --> 01:17:43.306
Aargh!

673
01:17:46.893 --> 01:17:48.895
Shit. Shit!

674
01:18:17.424 --> 01:18:18.925
Kill him!

675
01:18:20.552 --> 01:18:21.970
Kill him, Phil!

676
01:18:30.020 --> 01:18:31.479
Don't.

677
01:18:35.066 --> 01:18:36.943
Wuss.

678
01:18:54.669 --> 01:18:56.671
Hey!

679
01:18:57.839 --> 01:19:00.425
Where's Karen?

680
01:19:29.496 --> 01:19:31.915
Come on! Where the hell is she?

681
01:19:37.170 --> 01:19:41.091
They, uh...
They went back to her house.

682
01:19:41.257 --> 01:19:43.593
Where is her house?

683
01:19:54.270 --> 01:19:56.272
What the hell is that?

684
01:19:57.565 --> 01:20:00.777
- Hank?
- The dam. It's topped out!

685
01:20:07.575 --> 01:20:10.995
- How much time we got?
- Not long. It's an old dam.

686
01:20:14.833 --> 01:20:17.377
Then I guess you boys
better drop your guns.

687
01:20:20.672 --> 01:20:22.257
What?

688
01:20:23.842 --> 01:20:26.136
That's the deal.

689
01:20:27.887 --> 01:20:32.600
You let me and Hank go
with a few of these bags.

690
01:20:32.767 --> 01:20:35.729
Just a couple. I'm not greedy.

691
01:20:35.895 --> 01:20:39.399
- And I'll tell you where to find Karen.
- Get out of the boat.

692
01:20:40.191 --> 01:20:41.651
Hold on.

693
01:20:41.818 --> 01:20:43.194
- Hold on?
- Yeah.

694
01:20:43.361 --> 01:20:46.239
- It's the only way you're gonna find her.
- No.

695
01:20:46.406 --> 01:20:48.241
- It's only a couple of bags.
- No!

696
01:20:48.408 --> 01:20:50.785
- What do you mean, no?
- I mean no!

697
01:20:51.244 --> 01:20:54.414
I told you. I'm here for the money
and that's it!

698
01:20:57.125 --> 01:20:58.793
Boyd Street.

699
01:21:01.713 --> 01:21:04.382
She lives on Boyd Street.

700
01:21:05.508 --> 01:21:07.510
Three over.

701
01:21:09.012 --> 01:21:12.265
It's a two-storey with blue siding.

702
01:21:17.145 --> 01:21:19.230
Get out of the boat.

703
01:22:04.108 --> 01:22:06.903
What are you gonna do?

704
01:22:07.445 --> 01:22:09.447
You're just gonna leave us here?

705
01:22:10.698 --> 01:22:12.700
I oughta shoot you.

706
01:22:18.081 --> 01:22:20.625
Lord knows I ought to.

707
01:22:51.364 --> 01:22:53.366
Tom?

708
01:23:01.457 --> 01:23:03.459
I'm handcuffed.

709
01:23:07.547 --> 01:23:10.091
Yeah, you're handcuffed. Oh, boy.

710
01:23:10.258 --> 01:23:14.304
There's a saw in the kitchen,
in the cupboard next to the sink.

711
01:23:15.638 --> 01:23:18.892
Is that good or bad?

712
01:23:19.267 --> 01:23:21.269
That's very bad.

713
01:23:26.357 --> 01:23:28.735
You should've just killed me.

714
01:23:37.910 --> 01:23:39.787
The dam's gone. You gotta go.

715
01:23:41.789 --> 01:23:43.291
No!

716
01:23:43.875 --> 01:23:45.501
No!

717
01:23:46.544 --> 01:23:48.546
No!

718
01:23:55.845 --> 01:23:57.347
Go faster.

719
01:24:04.228 --> 01:24:06.230
We gotta go faster!

720
01:24:06.397 --> 01:24:08.858
Yeah... You're right.

721
01:24:43.184 --> 01:24:44.852
Oh, God!

722
01:25:06.582 --> 01:25:09.002
Aargh!

723
01:25:58.009 --> 01:26:00.178
- Well, that didn't work.
- Oh, God!

724
01:26:00.344 --> 01:26:01.637
Wait. The gun.

725
01:26:01.804 --> 01:26:03.347
- What gun?
- Wayne's gun.

726
01:26:03.514 --> 01:26:06.017
- Where is it?
- Try the porch.

727
01:26:59.278 --> 01:27:01.405
Come on, Henry!

728
01:27:01.572 --> 01:27:04.700
Forget about going to the light.

729
01:27:04.867 --> 01:27:08.120
Come back to me. You're all I've got.

730
01:27:11.124 --> 01:27:13.126
Oh, Henry. Thank God.

731
01:27:14.252 --> 01:27:17.213
The next time I say
"Let's evacuate",...

732
01:27:18.297 --> 01:27:20.216
..let's evacuate!

733
01:27:21.217 --> 01:27:23.219
Whatever you say, honey.

734
01:27:57.920 --> 01:28:00.173
It's the end of the line, kid!

735
01:28:16.898 --> 01:28:18.900
No, you don't.

736
01:29:29.136 --> 01:29:31.138
You all right?

737
01:29:32.223 --> 01:29:34.225
I'm really tired.

738
01:29:35.893 --> 01:29:38.646
But I guess I'll live.

739
01:29:39.271 --> 01:29:41.482
Thanks for comin' after us.

740
01:29:41.649 --> 01:29:43.859
You never learn, do you?

741
01:29:44.026 --> 01:29:46.612
I came for the money.

742
01:29:48.572 --> 01:29:49.198
Yeah.

743
01:31:24.335 --> 01:31:26.045
You OK?

744
01:31:27.046 --> 01:31:31.759
This is the State Police.
Cease fire and put down your weapons.

745
01:31:35.846 --> 01:31:37.848
You better get outta here.

746
01:31:44.188 --> 01:31:46.190
What about the money?

747
01:31:46.899 --> 01:31:49.944
- Gonna turn it in?
- Gotta turn it in.

748
01:32:36.449 --> 01:32:39.869
- Do you know if my church survived?
- Ah, your church.

749
01:32:40.035 --> 01:32:44.665
Last I saw there was... a little bit of
flood damage on the inside, but...

750
01:32:44.832 --> 01:32:46.959
But what?

751
01:32:47.126 --> 01:32:49.044
I'll give you the good news.

752
01:32:49.211 --> 01:32:51.755
The water from the dam
probably put the fire out.

753
01:32:51.922 --> 01:32:53.549
What fire?

754
01:32:53.716 --> 01:32:57.303
Listen. I had nothin' to do with it.
The sheriff started it.

755
01:32:57.470 --> 01:33:02.308
This is the State Police. Put your hands
behind your head and remain in view.

756
01:33:04.476 --> 01:33:07.480
- Was it a bad fire?
- Bad fire?

757
01:33:07.646 --> 01:33:09.732
No, no. It was a little fire.

758
01:33:09.899 --> 01:33:11.901
Some roof damage.

759
01:33:12.818 --> 01:33:17.323
They probably felt it safe to drive their
boats through the stained-glass windows.

760
01:33:17.656 --> 01:33:19.658
♪♪ Rain, rain, on my face

761
01:33:21.785 --> 01:33:24.872
♪♪ Hasn't stopped raining for days

762
01:33:26.457 --> 01:33:28.459
♪♪ My world is a flood

763
01:33:29.710 --> 01:33:31.462
♪♪ But slowly I become

764
01:33:31.629 --> 01:33:33.214
♪♪ At one with the mud

765
01:33:33.380 --> 01:33:37.301
♪♪ But if I can't swim after 40 days

766
01:33:37.468 --> 01:33:41.513
♪♪ And my mind is crushed
by the crashing waves

767
01:33:41.680 --> 01:33:45.684
♪♪ Lift me up so high that I cannot fall

768
01:33:45.851 --> 01:33:48.062
♪♪ Lift me, oh-oh

769
01:33:49.897 --> 01:33:51.565
♪♪ Lift me up

770
01:33:51.732 --> 01:33:54.026
♪♪ When I'm falling

771
01:33:54.193 --> 01:33:55.569
♪♪ Lift me up

772
01:33:55.736 --> 01:33:58.239
♪♪ I'm weak and I'm dying

773
01:33:58.405 --> 01:33:59.698
♪♪ Lift me up

774
01:33:59.865 --> 01:34:02.409
♪♪ I need you to hold me

775
01:34:02.576 --> 01:34:04.119
♪♪ Lift me up

776
01:34:04.286 --> 01:34:06.622
♪♪ Keep me from drowning again

777
01:34:06.789 --> 01:34:08.290
♪♪ Lift me, oh-oh

778
01:34:08.457 --> 01:34:10.751
♪♪ When I'm falling

779
01:34:10.918 --> 01:34:12.378
♪♪ Lift me, oh-oh

780
01:34:12.544 --> 01:34:15.089
♪♪ I'm weak and I'm dying

781
01:34:15.256 --> 01:34:16.674
♪♪ Lift me, oh-oh

782
01:34:16.840 --> 01:34:19.176
♪♪ I need you to hold me

783
01:34:19.343 --> 01:34:20.928
♪♪ Lift me, oh-oh

784
01:34:21.095 --> 01:34:24.139
♪♪ Keep me from drowning again
